      ],
      "impact": "The BST-SW bootstrap rail would droop severely each cycle so the buck's high-side MOSFET may not fully enhance; the +3V3 rail could fail to start or regulate, taking down the MCU, MAX31855 channels and status LED.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most reviewed connectivity (power mux TPS2121 IN1/IN2/ILIM/SS, AP63203 FB-to-3V3, heater switch U6 IN/DIAG_EN/CL/FAULT, three MAX31855 SPI/CS channels, USB-C CC dividers and 5.1k pulldowns) matches the specification, but the buck converter's bootstrap capacitor C13 is drawn as 100 pF instead of the ~0.1 uF required by the AP63203WU, which would prevent the 3.3 V rail from starting/regulating."
}

